Team2-api-data — central integration patch v2 (slices 2a, 3, 4a, 6)

Applies to /root/saas-rust (branch master). Apply from the repository root:

    git apply --check team2-api-data-central-20261031.v2.patch
    git apply       team2-api-data-central-20261031.v2.patch

SUPERSEDES v1 (sha256 af218702329fc4c1d330317f6fe3be822403a6e732f7c857aa23a8bf9559f5ab),
which covered slices 2a, 3 and 4a only. v1 is retained for history and still
applies cleanly on its own; use v2 for the whole team.

HARD PREREQUISITE — team1-billing-ai
  The `paid-order-reward` feature below references `referral-service`, and the
  slice-6 adapter imports `crate::utils::referral`, `crate::utils::referral_ledger`
  and `crate::schemas::referral_code`. None of those are declared in the current
  central files. team1 owns them; their wave-2C handoff
  (migration-notes/team1-wave2-c-handoff.md, "Central snippets - not applied")
  publishes them as position-agnostic snippets:
      referral-service = ["application-schemas", "mongo", "billing-service", "js-date", "dep:sha2"]
      utils/mod.rs   -> #[cfg(feature = "referral-service")] pub mod referral;
                        #[cfg(feature = "referral-service")] pub mod referral_ledger;
      schemas/mod.rs -> #[cfg(feature = "referral-service")]
                        #[path = "referral_code.schema.rs"] pub mod referral_code;
  Those snippets carry no line anchors, so they cannot conflict with the
  line-anchored hunks in this patch. Apply them alongside it. Until they land,
  the manifest references a feature that does not exist yet.

WHY A MERGED PATCH EXISTS
  The per-slice central patches in the individual handoff notes cannot be
  applied mechanically as written:
  1. Slices 2a and 4a insert their Cargo.toml feature at the SAME anchor (after
     `api-validation-route`), so each hunk's context is broken by the other's
     insertion and NEITHER ordering applies cleanly.
  2. Slice 3's Cargo.toml and schemas/mod.rs hunk headers carried context counts
     that did not match the lines in their hunks - arithmetically corrupt for
     `git apply`.
  3. Slice 2a's lib.rs hunk used a section heading instead of an explicit
     context block and its line offsets were stale.
  4. Slice 6's Cargo.toml feature also lands in the same manifest region.
  This file is the merged, conflict-free, count-correct equivalent of all four.

VERIFIED BEFORE PUBLISHING
  - Every hunk header count matches the lines actually present in its hunk.
  - Every insertion anchor was confirmed UNIQUE in its target file before the
    edit was applied.
  - `git apply --check` exits 0 against the current master tree for all four
    files. This was a READ-ONLY validation: the patch was NOT applied and the
    central files are unmodified in the working tree.
  - Every referenced Cargo feature and optional dependency was confirmed to
    exist in dimabot/Cargo.toml, except `referral-service`, which is team1's
    and is called out above as a hard prerequisite.
  - No new crate is added. No `[[test]]` entry is required for team2's suites:
    they self-gate with `#![cfg(feature = "...")]`.

